   407	## 5. Part (4): what an upper bound must look like, and whether one exists
   408	
   409	### 5.1 The exact shape
   410	
   411	At `W = 2` the profile is rigid: `W = s_1 mu_1` with `mu_1 >= 2` forces
   412	`(s_1,mu_1) = (1,2)`, so `S = 1`, `R = 0`, `a = N-2`, `D_gap = N-4`, and by `(C3)`
   413	the charge `a-1 = N-3` sits on at most `beta` points. Then
   414	
   415	```text
   416	   column W = 2 dies at every N   <==>   one proves   n_min <= C(N)  with
   417	        C(N) <= N - 2                     (unrestricted beta)
   418	        C(N) <= N - 1                     (restricted to the beta = 1 subcolumn)
   419	   equivalently, conditional on OPEN[MIN-EMBED-DEGREE] via DEG-DELTA(b),
   420	        delta_aff <= C_delta(N)  with  C_delta(N) <= ceil((N-1)/3) - 1.
   421	```
   422	
   423	So the required bound is **linear in `N` with slope exactly `1` and additive
   424	constant at most `-2`**. Slope `1` is not negotiable: at `W = 2`, MF-EXACT reads
   425	`n = N - 2 + 2 g_L + theta_inf`, so a bound `n <= cN + e` with `c < 1` would force
