   205	## 3. MERIDIAN-FLOOR
   206	
   207	**Verdict: CONFIRMED.**
   208	
   209	The proof at DG:312-328 is valid and can be made completely explicit.
   210	
   211	`F : A^2\E -> A^2\D` is a connected degree-`N` finite etale cover: B3E states
   212	this at 111-121, and the argument is standard from the definition of the
   213	non-properness set plus Keller etaleness. Connectedness gives transitive
   214	monodromy on the `N` sheets.
   215	
   216	A generic affine line meets the degree-`n` curve `D` in `n` points. Zariski's
   217	generic-line theorem gives a surjection from the line complement group to
   218	`pi_1(A^2\D)`, so the global group is generated by those `n` meridians. Since
   219	`D` is irreducible, the meridians are conjugate.
   220	
   221	The generic meridian cycle type is
   222	
   223	```text
   224	1^a * prod_l mu_l^{s_l}
   225	```
   226	
   227	with `W=N-a=sum_l s_l mu_l` and `S=sum_l s_l`. This is the same type used in
   228	MI's representation gate at 694-696 and in HORN's parity theorem: HR:73
   229	computes the sign from exactly `N-#cycles = W-S`. At `N=4`, MI's N4-PIN gives
   230	`(a,W,s,mu)=(2,2,1,2)`, hence generic cycle type `(2,1,1)`, matching
   231	MI:585-592 and HR:135-149. The local cusp and node types `(3,1)` and `(2,2)`
   232	are stronger local data; ORBIFOLD-CAGE uses those locally and does not change
   233	the generic-meridian floor.
   234	
   235	Block-count proof: begin with `N` singleton blocks. Adding one generator with
   236	cycle lengths `mu_l` can merge at most `sum_l s_l(mu_l-1)=W-S` blocks, because
   237	each cycle of length `r` can reduce the current block count by at most `r-1`.
   238	After all `n` meridian generators have been added, transitivity requires a
   239	single block. Thus
   240	
   241	```text
   242	n(W-S) >= N-1.
   243	```
   244	
   245	If `W-S=0`, no generator moves any sheet and transitivity fails for `N>1`; in
   246	the campaign regime 7.B' gives `mu_l>=2`, hence positivity anyway
   247	(MI:82-88). Since `S>=1`, `W-S <= W-1`, so
   248	
   249	```text
   250	n_min >= ceil((N-1)/(W-S)) >= ceil((N-1)/(W-1)).
   251	```
   252	
   253	**Cycle-typing check.** CUSP-PARITY uses this same generic meridian type and is
   254	compatible. ORBIFOLD-CAGE is local at a quasi-homogeneous cusp and is not a
   255	premise of the floor. No flag/place/series identification is present.
   256	
   257	**Half of `OPEN[N-VS-MAPDEG]`.** CD's Chau transfer gives the cap
   258	`n <= max(deg P,deg Q)` under its hypotheses (CD:119-126). Composing gives only
   259	
   260	```text
   261	max(deg P,deg Q) >= ceil((N-1)/(W-1)).
   262	```
   263	
   264	This is the lower half. It does not answer the needed upper bound of
   265	`OPEN[N-VS-MAPDEG]`.
