+floor and is the quantity I recomputed.
+
+## 5. B2 Forced Delta Values
+
+The B2 lower-delta computation combines LOC-MULT with
+`delta_P>=mult_P(mult_P-1)/2` and with DR:477-482, where a multibranch point
+carrying a singular branch contributes at least delta 2. MI:425-438 supplies
+the B2 thresholds: `beta>=2` for `5<=N<=10`, `beta>=1` for `11<=N<=16`.
+
+For the requested `N` values:
+
+```text
+N  death threshold | dB2 by W                         | min_W | W=2 value
+5        3         | W2: 6                            |   6   |    6
+6        3         | W2: 9                            |   9   |    9
+10       3         | W2:21, W3:9, W4:9                |   9   |   21
+11       1         | W2:24, W3:12, W4:6, W5:15        |   6   |   24
+16       1         | W2:39, W3:18, W4:12, W5:9,
+                    W6:9, W7:12                      |   9   |   39
+```
+
+Thus the producer's "6..39" sentence is correct for the `W=2` subcolumn
+across `N=5..16`; the cellwise B2 prices range lower when `W>2`. The
+directional conclusion is correct: these are lower bounds on `delta_aff`, so
+they cannot contradict the B2 death route, which requires upper bounds
+`delta_aff<=3` or `delta_aff<=1`. They price that route; they do not kill.
+
+## 6. W=2 Crossing
+
+At `W=2`, 7.B' forces `(s,mu)=(1,2)`, so `S=1`, `W-S=1`, `a=N-2`, and the
+meridian floor is `n>=N-1`. Therefore a floor-vs-ceiling kill of the whole
+unrestricted `W=2` column needs
+
+```text
+n_min <= C(N) <= N-2.
+```
+
+In the `beta=1` subcolumn, LOC-MULT improves the lower bound to `n>=N`, so
+there the threshold is `C(N)<=N-1`. MFS:416-420 is correct as a crossing price,
+but the word "only" must be read as "only by this route." DR:257-265 and
+DG:361-368 confirm that the reviewed material supplies only lower bounds on
+`D_F=max(deg P,deg Q)`, not an upper bound of this shape.
+
+## 7. Sharp-Chau
+
+Under the MF-EXACT hypotheses, the generic pencil curve `C_L` has degree
+`D_F=max(deg P,deg Q)`. A degree-`D_F` plane curve has at most `D_F` places at
+infinity. But the source-infinity bookkeeping above gives
+
+```text
+theta_L = nS + theta_inf.
+```
+
+Hence
+
+```text
+nS + theta_inf <= D_F,
+n <= (D_F-theta_inf)/S <= (D_F-1)/S,
+D_F >= nS+1 >= n+1.
+```
+
+This confirms MFS:451-465. Exact hypotheses: nonproper Keller map under H2,
+generic target coordinate `(u,v)`, no cancellation in `deg(u o F)=D_F`,
+generic line `L={u=gamma}`, generic meridian type from MI:82-88, and `S>=1`.
+It sharpens the Chau cap `n<=D_F`, especially when `S>1`, but it does not give
+the missing upper half of `OPEN[N-VS-MAPDEG]`.
+
+## Opens
+
+No new open is needed for this review. I carry the producer's two useful
+opens, with bounded quantities:
+
+```text
+OPEN[MF-DEFECT]
+  Question: is 2g_L + theta_inf >= 2 always for noninvertible Keller maps?
+  Bounded quantity: (g_L,theta_inf), with 0<=g_L<=p_a(D_F),
+  1<=theta_inf<=N, and nS+theta_inf<=D_F.
+
+OPEN[MULT-VS-BETA]
+  Question: at W=2 in B3, is beta=1 forced for N>=5?
+  Bounded quantity: beta in {1,...,a-1}={1,...,N-3}.
+```
+
+## Fallacy-v2 Check
+
+The review keeps separate `n`, `n_min`, `D_F`, `mrk(G)`, `mult_P`, `r_P`,
+`a_P`, `K_P`, `g_L`, and `g(E)`. MF-EXACT is an identity but not an attainment
+claim. `Phi` is a floor computed as a minimum over admissible configurations;
+it does not assert that any cell is realised by a Keller map. The group audit
+does not transfer case-(A) central statements into case (B3). No saturation,
+quotient normal form, raw remainder degree, or variable-ring map is used.
